{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_architecture_architecture_reference", "label": "Architecture Reference", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/architecture.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_architecture_index", "label": "index.ts", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture.html", "source_location": "Module map", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_architecture_server", "label": "server.ts", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture.html", "source_location": "Module map", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_architecture_allowlist", "label": "allowlist.ts", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture.html", "source_location": "Module map", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_architecture_health_gate", "label": "health-gate.ts", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture.html", "source_location": "Module map", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_architecture_daemon_client", "label": "daemon-client.ts", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture.html", "source_location": "Module map", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_architecture_normalize", "label": "normalize.ts", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture.html", "source_location": "Module map", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The single snake_case-to-camelCase boundary plus the memory excerpt redaction policy \u2014 normalization lives in one module so upstream casing quirks cannot leak into tool code."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_read_output", "label": "read-output.ts", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture.html", "source_location": "Module map", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Bounded polling reader with cursor guards and budgets; invariants: an event is consumed only once its text and pending state fit the budget (try before commit), a terminal session completes only after one further empty drain so racing trailing output is never dropped, and an error never discards text already produced."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_sanitizer", "label": "sanitizer.ts", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture.html", "source_location": "Output pipeline", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Eight-state terminal state machine that emits only on a newline reached in ground state so a split escape sequence can never leak; carriage return overwrites from line start so progress bars collapse to final state; pending state is compacted, never accumulated raw history, so a long-running progress bar cannot grow state without bound."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_resume_token", "label": "resume-token.ts", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture.html", "source_location": "Output pipeline", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_architecture_errors", "label": "errors.ts", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture.html", "source_location": "Module map", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The only shared leaf in the module graph; nothing else fans in, keeping the dependency graph acyclic and shallow."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_socket_path", "label": "socket-path.ts", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture.html", "source_location": "Module map", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_architecture_request_lifecycle", "label": "Request Lifecycle", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture.html", "source_location": "Request lifecycle", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every tool call runs the same six stages (schema validation, health gate, authorization, transport, normalization/output pipeline, result shaping); stages 1-3 can reject without touching the daemon, which is what makes Guards a trust boundary."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_output_pipeline", "label": "Output Pipeline", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture.html", "source_location": "Output pipeline", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_architecture_security_model", "label": "Security Model", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture.html", "source_location": "Security model", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Narrowing the authority an LLM inherits is the point of the project, not a feature of it; controls are deny-by-default, fail-fast configuration, authoritative-record authorization, path-component containment, fail-closed lookups, excerpt redaction, and no sensitive logging \u2014 while explicitly not guaranteeing a sandbox, semantic sanitization, token encryption, or protection from same-user bypass."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_upstream_contract", "label": "Upstream Contract", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture.html", "source_location": "Upstream contract", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Pinned to OpenCoven/coven 1fe9a744 (CLI 0.0.34); six live-verified behaviors are each absorbed at a single boundary module so they cannot leak into tool code."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_architecture_index", "target": "docs_architecture_allowlist", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_fi